{{Codex|Forged by a master gunsmith, this Tenno burst rifle will strike down targets with swift precision.}}

The '''Tiberon''' is a [[Tenno]]-made three round burst-fire rifle. Compared to most burst-fire rifles, the Tiberon is much more accurate and primarily deals {{D|Puncture}} damage, albeit at the cost of reduced [[status chance]].

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Puncture}} damage.
*Can use the Tiberon-exclusive {{M|Critical Precision}} mod.
*Can equip the Tiberon-exclusive {{M|Measured Burst}} mod ([[Conclave]] only).
*Comes with a {{Pol|Madurai}} polarity.

{{Advantages|class=Rifle|trigger=Burst|
*Very low recoil.
*Third highest [[fire rate]] of all burst-fire rifles, behind {{Weapon|Paracyst}} and {{Weapon|Burston Prime}}.
}}

{{Disadvantages|class=Rifle|trigger=Burst|
*Linearly less efficient &ndash; sometimes a target may only die with four bullets, which requires an entire second burst to be fired.
}}

{{WeaponComparison|Tiberon Prime}}

==Acquisition==
The Tiberon's blueprint can be purchased from the [[Market]].

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}
This weapon can be sold for '''7,500'''.

==Notes==
*Like the Sybaris, the Tiberon's burst has a very tight shot grouping, which combined with its high base accuracy and negligible recoil makes it better at long-range shooting than other burst-fire weapons, such as the {{Weapon|Burston}} or {{Weapon|Hind}}.
*The Tiberon is a very strong candidate for a tenno [[Specter]] to use thanks to its high damage per second combined with high accuracy.
*Has a higher damage per bullet than other low-tier burst fire weapons, like Burston or Hind.

==Trivia==
*The weapon's name may be derived from ''[[wiktionary:tiburón#Spanish|tiburón]]'', the Spanish word for ''shark''. Its design also appears to take cues from the animal, particularly the "blades" beneath the muzzle which resemble a shark's pectoral fins.
*The Tiberon is the first weapon outside of Clan [[Research]] that requires a [[Forma]] to construct.
*At the time of its release, the {{Weapon|Latron Prime}} or the {{Weapon|Latron Wraith}} could also be used to build the Tiberon. This was fixed in {{ver|14.9.1}}.
*Intriguingly, crafting the Tiberon requires the Latron, a semi-automatic rifle, instead of another burst-fire rifle, such as the Burston. The discrepancy can also be explained by the fact that Tiberon sports 3 separate barrels, with presumably one shot being fired from each, thus each barrel technically is its own semi-automatic weapon.
*The Tiberon is reloaded by removing the magazine which is located at the butt end of the stock.

