'''Tenet Quanta''' is the [[Tenet]] variant of the {{Weapon|Quanta}} laser cutter, sporting increased damage, [[Critical Chance]], [[Critical Multiplier]], [[Status Chance]], and [[Magazine]], but with marginally lower [[Fire Rate]].

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals {{D|Electricity}} damage on its Primary Fire and {{D|Blast}} damage on its [[Alternate Fire]].
*Primary Fire shoots two concentrated continuous beams.
**Innate [[multishot]] of 2 beams.
**Consumes 0.5 ammo per tick of damage.
**Pinpoint [[accuracy]].
***{{M|Heavy Caliber}}'s accuracy penalty is minimal.
*[[Alternate Fire]] lobs a small cube that explodes in '''0.5''' meter radius on contact or after being left alone for '''9''' seconds. If damaged by any player in any way (e.g. explosion of a nearby cube), it explodes in '''6''' meter radius.
**Does not inflict [[Stagger|self-stagger]] and has no [[Damage Falloff]].
**Initial hit and explosion apply status separately.
**Explosion does not need direct line of sight to deal damage and will penetrate walls.
**Consume '''10''' rounds per shot.
*Innate {{Pol|Vazarin}}, {{Pol|Madurai}}, and {{Pol|Naramon}} polarities.
*Adversary Weapon:
**Comes with an additional bonus {{D|Impact}}, {{D|Heat}}, {{D|Cold}}, {{D|Electricity}}, {{D|Toxin}}, {{D|Magnetic}}, or {{D|Radiation}} damage, based on the Kuva Lich's [[Adversary System/Progenitor|progenitor Warframe]], which increases the listed base damage of the weapon by 25%-60%.
***[[Valence Fusion]] can optionally change the resulting output damage type, and can upgrade the bonus increase (up to 60%).
**[[Polarization|Polarizing]] the weapon increases its max [[rank]] by '''2''', capping at rank '''40''' after '''5''' polarizations, granting the weapon additional mod capacity.
**{{Resource|Elemental Vice}} can be applied to the weapon after it has reached rank 40, allowing the bonus damage type to be swapped freely.
**Listed [[Mastery Rank]] requirement is not enforced - the weapon may theoretically be obtained at any mastery rank by acquiring and vanquishing a Kuva Lich that has this weapon equipped.

{{Advantages|class=Rifle|trigger=Held|
}}

{{Disadvantages|class=Rifle|trigger=Held|
*Primary Fire:
**Damage ramps up from 30% to 100% over 0.6 seconds when firing. After firing stops for 0.8 seconds, the damage decays back to 30% over 2 seconds.
**Limited range of 50 meters.
*Alternate Fire:
**Cubes have slow travel time and a limited range of roughly 15 meters.
**Explosion has a [[Enemy Body Parts|headshot]] multiplier of 1x and cannot trigger headshot conditions.
}}
